{{Otheruses|the free-to-play guide|the members' guide|Pay-to-play Fishing training}}

There are several ways to train [[Fishing]] in [[free-to-play]]. Depending on the desired goals of the player, they can choose between methods favouring experience rates or profit. If you choose to go with making a profit, be sure to sell your catch at the [[Grand Exchange]] and not a General store in order to maximize your profits. Keep in mind, since the [[Grand Exchange]] acts as an in-game stock market, that means the prices are always changing. You can find the latest prices on the [[Grand Exchange]] [[RuneScape:Grand Exchange Market Watch/Fishing#Raw fish|here]].

==Methods with the highest experience rates==
===Levels 1–20 – Raw shrimps and raw anchovies===
{{plinkp|raw shrimps|pic=raw shrimps}} {{plinkp|raw anchovies|pic=raw anchovies}} Fishing [[raw shrimps]] and [[raw anchovies]] with a [[small fishing net]] at a [[net fishing]] location is the fastest way to train fishing at level 1 with experience rates of 1,500–3,000 experience per hour. The [[Fishing spot (small net, bait)|small net fishing spot]] is the only possible fishing location at level 1. Players must reach level 15 Fishing before there is a chance for them to receive a raw anchovy while fishing, which will increase their experience rates to around 7,500 experience per hour. To achieve the most optimal experience rates, players would want to drop the caught fish, instead of banking. Alternatively, the raw fish can be cooked for small amounts of [[Cooking]] experience. If planning on banking the fish, players should fish at [[Al Kharid]], due to its proximity to a bank, however there is an aggressive level 14 [[scorpion]] that occasionally wanders near the southern fishing spots. Another spot to bank the fish is south of the bank in [[Draynor Village]], next to the willow trees, though beware of aggressive level 7 [[Dark wizard|Dark Wizards]]. For players that don't want to have to deal with combat, and want to sell the fish, the fishing spot South-West of [[Port Sarim]] is ideal as it is a somewhat short run away from [[Gerrant's Fishy Business.]]

===Alternative for levels 5–20 – raw sardines and raw herring===
{{plinkp|raw sardine|pic=raw sardine}} {{plinkp|raw herring|pic=raw herring}} Fishing [[raw sardine]] and [[raw herring]] with a [[fishing rod]] and [[bait]] at a [[bait fishing]] location is the fastest way to train fishing until level 20 with experience rate of 3,000-8,000 experience per hour (when herring is unlocked it is 8,000). The [[Fishing spot (small net, bait)|small net fishing spot]] is the ideal place to fish. Players who reach level 20 fishing can move to fishing [[trout]] for faster experience per hour.

===Levels 20–40/99 – Raw trout and raw salmon===
{{plinkp|raw trout|pic=raw trout}} {{plinkp|raw salmon|pic=raw salmon}} Fishing [[raw trout]] and [[raw salmon]] with a [[fly fishing rod]] and [[feather|feathers]] at a [[Fishing#Fly fishing rods and feathers|fly fishing]] location before dropping the caught fish offers the fastest way to train Fishing to 99 in free-to-play. At level 20, players can expect to achieve around 13k XP/hour while dropfishing due to only catching raw trout. At level 30, there is a chance to receive raw salmon while fishing, which will increase their experience rates to around 25k XP/hour while dropfishing.

Fly fishing can be done in [[Lumbridge]] quickly reached via [[canoe]] or [[cowbell amulet]], and in [[Barbarian Village]] quickly reached via canoe or [[skull sceptre]]. Each catch consumes a feather which results in around 600 feathers consumed from levels 20–40 and 225,000 feathers from 20–99.

Players can train both Fishing and [[Cooking]] by cooking the fish near their fishing spot before dropping the fish or only dropping the [[burnt fish]] if banking. The most convenient location to do this is by using the permanent fire in Barbarian Village next to the fishing spot. If fishing in Lumbridge, players can instead bring an [[axe]] and [[tinderbox]] to build their own fire. The nearby [[Barfy Bill]] can store an axe but if one is needed, a bronze axe spawns in the [[logs (bronze axe)|stump]] north at [[Groats' farm]].

* Method #1: Fly fish at Barbarian Village, cook at Barbarian Village permanent fire, bank cooked fish at [[Ferox Enclave]] (57 [[Woodcutting]] needed for [[waka canoe]], canoe from Barbarian Village to Ferox Enclave for banking, and canoe back to Barbarian Village to fish): ~18k Fishing XP/hour & ~24k Cooking XP/hour

* Method #2: Fly fish at Barbarian Village or Lumbridge, bank raw fish at Ferox Enclave (57 Woodcutting needed for waka canoe, canoe from Barbarian Village or Lumbridge to Ferox Enclave for banking, and canoe back to Barbarian Village or Lumbridge to fish): ~26k Fishing XP/hour

* Method #3: Fly fish at Barbarian Village, cook at Barbarian Village permanent fire, drop cooked fish: ~23.5k Fishing XP/hour & ~31k Cooking XP/hour.

Fish can be caught using [[Tick_manipulation#3-tick_Fishing|tick manipulation]] by collecting [[snow]] spawned by [[reindeer hat]] or [[snow globe]] (requires having completed a [[Christmas event]]), by using a [[needle]] on [[leather]] (or vice versa) with [[thread]] in the inventory while holding space or another key to clear the Make-X interface which will also effectively delay the skilling timer by a slightly slower four ticks (but doesn't require a Christmas event), or by eating their cooked versions, resulting in significantly higher experience rates at the cost of increased intensity.

